{:edb/db-before-t 830 :edb/db-after-t 831 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534143 50 #inst "2026-10-06T04:31:59.685Z" 13194139534143 true] [17592186087511 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/assets/1c498dcdef2a71cc27117c2c0a43dd54074128ec3e5693e13a12d18b660d1cf4.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of the cubic polynomial $f(x).$ Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $1.$" 13194139534143 true] [17592186087511 1100 "The Argand diagram above shows the roots of the cubic polynomial $f(x)$. Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $1$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/896/Source/Images/19c7ba3bb7e7f5410bb6fd0adf39ce0e.png)" 13194139534143 false] [17592186087511 1145 "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}x_1= 2}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}x_{2,3}=-2\\pm \\textrm{i}}\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}a=1}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x) &= a(x - x_{1})(x - x_{2})(x - x_{3}) \\\\\n&= (x - 2)(x - (-2 + \\textrm{i}))(x - (-2 - \\textrm{i}))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x - 2)(x - (-2 + \\textrm{i}))(x - (-2 - \\textrm{i})) &=  \\\\\n(x - 2)(x^{2} - x(-2 - \\textrm{i}) - x(-2 + \\textrm{i}) + (-2 + \\textrm{i})(-2 - \\textrm{i})) &=  \\\\\n(x - 2)(x^{2} + 4x + 5) &=  \\\\\nx^{3} + 4x^{2} + 5x - 2x^{2} - 8x - 10 &=  \\\\\n&= x^{3} + 2x^{2} - 3x - 10 \\mid\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nf(x) = x^3+2x^2-3x-10\n$$" 13194139534143 false] [17592186087511 1145 "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${\\color{black}x_1= 2}$ and ${\\color{black}x_{2,3}=-2\\pm \\textrm{i}}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is ${\\color{black}a=1}.$ \n\nTherefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =(x-2)(x-(-2+\\text{i}))(x-(-2-\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)(x-(-2+\\text{i}))(x-(-2-\\text{i})) & = \\\\ (x-2)({x}^{2}-x(-2-\\text{i})-x(-2+\\text{i})+(-2+\\text{i})(-2-\\text{i})) & = \\\\ (x-2)({x}^{2}+4x+5) & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+5x-2{x}^{2}-8x-10 & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-3x-10 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x) = x^3+2x^2-3x-10.$" 13194139534143 true] [17592186087586 1100 "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots $x_1=x_2=2,x_3=1$, and the coefficient of the cubic term is $3$. Find $P(x)$." 13194139534143 false] [17592186087586 1100 "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots $x_1=x_2=2,x_3=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $3.$ Find $P(x).$" 13194139534143 true] [17592186087586 1145 "Since our cubic polynomial has roots\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}x_1=x_2=2}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}x_3=1}\n$$\n\nand the coefficient of the cubic term is\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}a=3}\n$$\n\nwe can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na(x - x_{1})(x - x_{2})(x - x_{3}) &= 3(x - 2)(x - 2)(x - 1)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3(x - 2)(x - 2)(x - 1) &= 3(x^{2} - 4x + 4)(x - 1) \\\\\n&= 3(x^{3} - x^{2} - 4x^{2} + 4x + 4x - 4) \\\\\n&= 3(x^{3} - 5x^{2} + 8x - 4) \\\\\n&= 3x^{3} - 15x^{2} + 24x - 12\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(x) = 3x^3 -15x^2+24x-12\n$$" 13194139534143 false] [17592186087586 1145 "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${\\color{black}x_1=x_2=2}$ and ${\\color{black}x_3=1},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is ${\\color{black}a=3},$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =3(x-2)(x-2)(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x-2)(x-2)(x-1) & =3({x}^{2}-4x+4)(x-1) \\\\  & =3({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-4{x}^{2}+4x+4x-4) \\\\  & =3({x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+8x-4) \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}-15{x}^{2}+24x-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x) = 3x^3 -15x^2+24x-12.$" 13194139534143 true] [17592186087697 1020 #edb/ref 17592186278514 13194139534143 true] [17592186087697 1020 #edb/ref 17592186278528 13194139534143 true] [17592186087697 1020 #edb/ref 17592186278535 13194139534143 true] [17592186087697 1020 #edb/ref 17592186278542 13194139534143 true] [17592186087697 1020 #edb/ref 17592186278559 13194139534143 true] [17592186087753 1020 #edb/ref 17592186278507 13194139534143 true] [17592186087753 1020 #edb/ref 17592186278521 13194139534143 true] [17592186087753 1020 #edb/ref 17592186278552 13194139534143 true] [17592186087906 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534143 true] [17592186087906 1100 "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots $x_{1} = x_{2} =-1, x_{3} = 3$, and the coefficient of the cubic term is $2$. Find $P(x)$." 13194139534143 false] [17592186087906 1100 "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-1,{x}_{3}=3,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $2.$ Find $P(x).$" 13194139534143 true] [17592186087906 1145 "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-1$ and ${x}_{3}=3,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =2(x-(-1))(x-(-1))(x-3) \\\\  & =2(x+1)(x+1)(x-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x+1)(x+1)(x-3) & =2({x}^{2}+2x+1)(x-3) \\\\  & =2({x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+2{x}^{2}-6x+x-3) \\\\  & =2({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-5x-3) \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-10x-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-10x-6.$" 13194139534143 true] [17592186087915 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534143 true] [17592186087915 1100 "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots $x_{1} =-5$, $x_{2} = 0$, and $x_{3} = 1$, and the coefficient of the cubic term is $-2$. Find $P(x)$." 13194139534143 false] [17592186087915 1100 "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-5,$ ${x}_{2}=0,$ and ${x}_{3}=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $-2.$ Find $P(x).$" 13194139534143 true] [17592186087915 1145 "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=-5,$ ${x}_{1}=0,$ and ${x}_{3}=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =-2(x-(-5))(x-0)(x-1) \\\\  & =-2x(x+5)(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x(x+5)(x-1) & =-2x({x}^{2}+4x-5) \\\\  & =-2({x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5x) \\\\  & =-2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+10x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=-2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+10x.$" 13194139534143 true] [17592186278507 1017 #edb/ref 17592186278508 13194139534143 true] [17592186278507 1089 "q-104471" 13194139534143 true] [17592186278507 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534143 true] [17592186278507 1100 "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-3,{x}_{3}=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $5.$ Find $P(x).$" 13194139534143 true] [17592186278507 1113 #uuid "96760cb6-c1a1-5102-a49a-28f41c5afd39" 13194139534143 true] [17592186278507 1145 "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-3$ and ${x}_{3}=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=5,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =5(x-(-3))(x-(-3))(x-1) \\\\  & =5(x+3)(x+3)(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(x+3)(x+3)(x-1) & =5({x}^{2}+6x+9)(x-1) \\\\  & =5({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+6{x}^{2}-6x+9x-9) \\\\  & =5({x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+3x-9) \\\\  & =5{x}^{3}+25{x}^{2}+15x-45.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=5{x}^{3}+25{x}^{2}+15x-45.$" 13194139534143 true] [17592186278508 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278509 13194139534143 true] [17592186278508 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278510 13194139534143 true] [17592186278508 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278511 13194139534143 true] [17592186278508 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278512 13194139534143 true